    "sentence_translations": [
      "Shanghai South",
      "",
      "Little Chen was working at the train station.",
      "One day, an old grandma asked him: “Young man, how do I go to Shanghai South?”",
      "Little Chen saw that the old grandma couldn’t move very well, ..",
      ".. so he helped her go through the VIP lounge, and escorted her all the way onto the train going to Hainan.",
      "As a result, the old grandma’s child waited the entire day at Shanghai South without being able to meet her.",
      "",
      "Chinese is very fascinating. Depending on how you separate the words, the meaning will be different.",
      "Like this “Shang Hai Nan”. It can be understood as “Shang / Hainan”, meaning “Go to Hainan”;",
      "It can also be understood as “Shanghai / Nan”, an abbreviation for “Shanghai South Station”.",
      "The old grandma wanted to go to Shanghai South Station, but Little Chen thought she wanted to go to Hainan.",
      "As a result, he made her a great disservice despite good intentions.",
